 fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Kevin Stitt (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kevin Stitt is term-limited, leaving Oklahoma's governorship open in a state that leans Republican by seventeen points. Republicans nominated Mike Mazzei, who edged Gentner Drummond in a runoff with President Trump's backing; Democrats nominated Cyndi Munson, with three independents also on the ballot.\n\nPublic polling of the general election has not surfaced, so the picture rests on fundamentals: the state's heavy Republican lean, unanimous Solid or Safe Republican ratings from six expert outlets, and prediction markets giving Munson roughly seven to eight percent. Mazzei's narrow runoff win leaves some party consolidation to finish, and Munson is campaigning on a change message, while a planned Trump rally aims to energize Republican turnout. The race is rated Safe Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -13.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0251, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0363, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.5}]}